Completeness:
    - Program collects raw counts from training set for Viterbi probabilities       - Complete
    - Viterbi algorithm impmplemented                                               - Complete
    - Training set tags are predicted                                               - Complete
    - Results are evalutated                                                        - Complete

    The program is fully Complete

System Accuracy (Viterbi): 87.83%
System Accuracy (Baseline): 87.24%

Three Errors (found in the predicted tags correspondig to the last three sentences of the training corpus):
    1. Incorrect verb and participle tags - The possilbe reason for this mistake is the model may
       have learned misleading word-tag associations or transition probabilities from the training
       corpus.
    2. Singular versus plural nouns - The model may have learned that the word is more frequently used 
       as a singular noun (NN) than as a plural noun (NNS). Because the model relies on learned emission 
       and transition probabilities, it may choose the singular tag even when the sentence's grammatical 
       context supports a plural noun.
    3. Currency Symbol misclassified as noun - The model may have learned an insufficient or misleading 
       association between the currency symbol and its tag. In the training data, numerical expressions 
       can appear in different contexts, and the model may not have learned the specific annotation convention 
       used for this example. The currency symbol is annotated as CD in the ground truth, but the model 
       predicts $.
